{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cleancut-everyday-anole","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Extract interpret_failure() -- run()'s except spine\n\nADR 0055 decision 3, FIRST extraction. The ordering is deliberate and was corrected by adversarial\nreview.\n\n## Why this one first\n\nAn earlier draft ordered resolution first, claiming \"every\" recent commit touching runner.py was a\npre-call resolution concern. Review disproved it -- at least five were not: 8e4d6a46d and 5144a9009\n(usage/cost, post-call), 4291b9a56 (disposition classifier, in the except arm), 3938c7ed2 (gate\nposture, in preflight), c8aa1ecdd (refusal fail-closed, in the call section). The real figure is ~70%.\n\nThe except spine is also the DENSEST code region in the file: 75 lines at only 20% comment (58 code),\nversus the pre-call region's 50% comment (113 code across 254 lines). Per line extracted it returns\nthe most headroom, and it is where several of the most recent growth commits actually landed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/runner.py:507-581 -> `interpret_failure(...)` with explicit parameters\n  (exc, run_messages, req_limit, eff_max_iter, and whatever the arms genuinely read).\n- Preserve the three arms' ORDER: UsageLimitExceeded, LLMError, then broad Exception. The broad arm\n  tries translate_sampling_parameter_rejection FIRST; that ordering is load-bearing.\n- tests/unit/\n\nNOTE for the implementer: translate_sampling_parameter_rejection performs NO retry -- it inspects and\nreclassifies. An earlier architecture draft wrongly described it as rebuilding settings and retrying.\nIt does not break the resolve-then-execute shape.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier: pure given an exception and the counters.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts a sampling-parameter rejection is reclassified to the typed config error and NOT\n      to LLMUnavailableError -- the arm-ordering property; it fails if the broad classification runs first\n- [ ] a test asserts the raised TYPE is unchanged for each of the three arms, so every existing\n      `except LLMUnavailableError` caller keeps working\n- [ ] the classified disposition is still attached as METADATA without changing the raised type\n- [ ] runner.py's before/after LOC is recorded in the commit message\n- [ ] any monkeypatch target that moved is repointed IN THE SAME COMMIT and named in the message with\n      its reason (see the parent's note on the six known targets)\n","id":"e6bd-8fd3-3c2d-4435","parent_id":"7f86-d935-3742-476a","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Extract interpret_failure() from run()'s except spine"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785510698883889001,"uuid":"35f57ae8-9b6e-43c6-97a7-b121602e4830"}